@ahmadalfy @tom_doerr Part 1
The repo does a few things:
- syntax and static validation like is the email following RFC-5322 or now. It is generic email like admin@, no-reply@, sales@, etc. it also check if the email is part of or flagged as disposable email address (DEA) like mailnator

@ahmadalfy @tom_doerr Part 2
- domain DNS records check against MX records
- then it does a reachability test based on the provider identified from the DNS MX records then using the actual SMTP protocol, it checks if the mailing server will reply back with 200 email exist or 550 unknown user

@ahmadalfy @tom_doerr Part 3

or any other errors
- sometimes the above step doesn’t always work so like with a provider like Yahoo who blocks these SMTP connection out of the box or just always give us 200

